STEP 13 — EPIC 3: Citizen complaint intake (public portal)

What was built:
- Public form /kerkese "Paraqit kërkesë ose ankesë" (Figma 44:2): 5 numbered
  sections — 1 type (Kërkesë / Ankesë) + automatic date, 2 applicant data,
  3 case details (location + description), 4 optional files (dropzone, list
  with Shkarko / remove), 5 truthfulness declaration with the name filled in
  from section 2 + required checkbox. "Konfirmo dhe dërgo" / "Pastro
  formularin". No login: citizens have no account.
- Confirmation page /kerkese/konfirmim/{numri} (Figma 24:99) with the
  tracking number and "Çfarë ndodh më pas".
- Tracking page /gjurmo and /gjurmo/{numri} (Figma 25:2): status pill +
  5-step timeline. Links to it in the portal header and the landing page.
- The same validation rules (Albanian messages) in the browser and on the
  server; the form cannot be sent until everything required is valid and the
  declaration is checked.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------
ENDPOINTS
-------------------------------------------------------------------------
Public (no login):
    POST /kerkesa                  multipart/form-data: the form fields + files
        fields: lloji (kerkese|ankese), emri, mbiemri, numri_personal,
                email (optional), telefoni, adresa (optional), lokacioni,
                pershkrimi, deklarata_pranuar (true), files (0–10 files)
        201 -> { numri_gjurmimit, status: "e_re", created_at }
        422 -> { detail: [ { loc: ["body", <field>], msg } ] }  (Albanian messages)
    GET  /kerkesa/gjurmo/{numri}   public status, NO personal data:
        { numri_gjurmimit, lloji, status, created_at,
          timeline: [ { titulli, gjendja: kryer|aktual|pritje, koha } ] }
        404 -> "Nuk u gjet asnjë kërkesë me këtë numër"
Staff only (JWT, any role):
    GET  /attachments/{id}/download   the stored file (401 without login).
    Citizens' files are personal data, so this is not public. In the form,
    "Shkarko" downloads the file that is still in the browser (before sending).

Why one multipart request (fields + files together): the submission is
all-or-nothing. If any field or file is invalid, nothing is saved; with a
separate upload endpoint, files from abandoned forms would be left behind.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------
RULES (browser and server)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------
    lloji            required: kerkese / ankese
    emri, mbiemri    required, max 80, must contain a letter
    numri personal   exactly 10 digits (spaces ignored)
    email            optional, valid, max 120
    telefoni         required, digits with optional + ( ) - spaces, 6–15 digits
    adresa           optional, max 255
    lokacioni        required, max 255
    pershkrimi       required, max 5000 (line breaks kept)
    deklarata        must be accepted
    files            optional, PDF / JPG / PNG, max 10 MB each, max 10 files
Server-side cleaning: Unicode NFC, trimmed, control characters removed,
repeated spaces collapsed. The declaration name ("Arben Krasniqi") is built by
the server from emri + mbiemri, not taken from the browser.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------
DATABASE — migration 0002 (backend/migrations/versions/0002_kerkesa_intake.py)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------
Adds to `kerkesat`:
    lloji ENUM('kerkese','ankese') NOT NULL
    aplikuesi_emri VARCHAR(80), aplikuesi_mbiemri VARCHAR(80)
    aplikuesi_numri_personal VARCHAR(10)
    aplikuesi_email VARCHAR(120) NULL
    aplikuesi_telefoni VARCHAR(30)
    aplikuesi_adresa VARCHAR(255) NULL
    deklarata_pranuar BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT FALSE
    deklarata_emri VARCHAR(160)
The old raportuesi_emri / raportuesi_kontakti / anonim columns are kept but
not used by the portal (other channels may use them later). Each submission
also creates a `lokacionet` row (kerkesat.lokacion_id) and one `attachments`
row per file. kanali = 'portal', status = 'e_re'; category, urgency etc. stay
empty — they are filled later (AI / staff).

Commands (from inside backend\):
    venv\Scripts\python.exe -m alembic upgrade head     -> apply 0002
    venv\Scripts\python.exe -m alembic downgrade -1     -> remove the 0002 columns
    venv\Scripts\python.exe -m alembic current          -> should say 0002 (head)

-------------------------------------------------------------------------
TRACKING NUMBER
-------------------------------------------------------------------------
    VU-{year}-{sequence}   e.g. VU-2026-0001, VU-2026-0002 …
The sequence restarts every year, has at least 4 digits (VU-2026-12345 after
9999) and is the highest number of that year + 1. The UNIQUE index on
numri_gjurmimit protects against two submissions at the same moment (the
second one retries with the next number). Tracking is case-insensitive.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------
FILE STORAGE
-------------------------------------------------------------------------
    backend\uploads\kerkesat\{kerkesa_id}\{random-32-hex}.{pdf|jpg|png}
- Folder set by UPLOAD_DIR in backend\.env (default backend\uploads). It is in
  .gitignore: citizens' files are never committed.
- The citizen's file name is never used. The type is decided from the file's
  first bytes (a .pdf that is not really a PDF is refused).
- attachments.lloji = 'dokument' (PDF) or 'foto' (JPG/PNG);
  attachments.path = the path relative to UPLOAD_DIR.
- If saving fails, the files written for that submission are removed.
- Tests use a temporary folder, never backend\uploads.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------
HOW TO RUN
-------------------------------------------------------------------------
    cd backend ; venv\Scripts\python.exe -m alembic upgrade head
    cd backend ; venv\Scripts\python.exe -m uvicorn app.main:app --reload --port 8000
    cd frontend ; npm run dev
Then open http://localhost:5173/kerkese (or 5174) — no login needed.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------
HOW TO TEST   (all layers: docs/12)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------
From the project root:
    backend\venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pytest test\unit\test_kerkesa_unit.py
    backend\venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pytest test\integration\test_kerkesa.py
    backend\venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pytest test\e2e\test_kerkesa_ui.py
    cd frontend ; npm test
What they check:
- unit: text cleaning, every form rule, file-type detection by content,
  size limit, tracking-number format, timeline per status.
- integration: valid submission -> 201 + kerkesa + lokacion + attachments +
  files on disk; each missing / invalid field -> 422; declaration not
  accepted -> 422; wrong type (incl. a fake .pdf), >10 MB, >10 files -> 422
  and nothing saved; files removed if saving fails; two submissions get
  different (sequential) numbers; tracking shows the status and NO personal
  data; unknown number -> 404; download: staff 200, anonymous 401, paths
  outside the upload folder refused.
- frontend (Vitest): the rules block an empty / invalid form, a valid form
  passes, file checks.
- Selenium: the 5 sections; empty submit shows the errors and sends nothing;
  specific messages; declaration required; name and type fill in live; wrong
  file type refused; Shkarko / remove on attached files; a fake PDF rejected
  by the server and shown in the form; happy path with 2 files -> tracking
  number -> tracking page shows E RE + timeline and no personal data;
  "Pastro formularin"; unknown and badly formatted tracking numbers.

Result at the end of this step: 225 backend tests (84 unit, 92 integration,
49 Selenium) and 38 frontend unit tests pass; migration upgrade / downgrade /
upgrade and "alembic check" clean.

New dependencies: python-multipart (backend), lucide-react (frontend icons).
